hello and welcome to the introductory  lesson of the smack course offered by  simply learn smack abbreviated as social  mobile analytics and cloud is an  upcoming business model in many  organizations this lesson provides an  introduction to the course the next  screen displays the key features of  simply learn offerings before you start  please spend some time and go through  the key features of simply learned  offerings displayed on the screen let us  look at the objectives of this course in  the next screen by the end of this  course you will be able to describe SMAC  and its scope you will also be able to  explain SMAT components and their scope  respectively in the next screen we will  focus on the course overview as you may  be aware social mobile analytics and  cloud are individual technologies  however in recent years they have  emerged as an integrated whole called  smack stack this training course  provides information on social media  marketing and its impact on business the  mobile platform and its uses in various  industries big data and analytics in  businesses and cloud computing and its  benefits to organizations simply learns  smack course also lists various  certification and non certification  courses available in the social media  mobile analytics cloud computing fields  respectively we will look into the  target audience for this course in the  next screen the SMAC course is aimed at  professionals aspiring for a career in  any of the smack related fields the  primary target audience for this course  are consultants IT professionals sales  and marketing professionals technical  managers and project managers students  and other aspirants who wish to gain a  thorough understanding of SMAC can also  benefit from this course let us discuss  the prerequisites to take up courses  under each SMAC component in the  subsequent screen  simply learns smack course can be taken  up by any individual who wishes to gain  an understanding of smack however  components in the smack course have  separate prerequisites to complete them  the prerequisites for the courses in  each of the smack components that is  social media mobile analytics and cloud  are displayed in the table the  prerequisites to complete the social  media courses are basic knowledge of the  Internet ability to use popular search  engines and working knowledge of the MS  Office suite such as word spreadsheet  and PowerPoint  the prerequisites for mobile marketing  courses are similar to the social media  courses however a basic knowledge of  using mobile apps is required the  prerequisites for analytics courses  include fundamental knowledge of any  programming language  basic knowledge of Linux and fundamental  programming skills working knowledge of  Java may be required however it is not  mandatory to take up cloud computing  courses you must have 24 to 36 months of  work experience in IT networking network  storage system administration or data  center administration you also must be  familiar with any of the major  hypervisors for server virtualization  though vendor specific certifications in  virtualization are not required in the  next screen we will discuss how the SMAC  course could add value to professionals  SMAC professionals can use social media  in their job roles to reach larger  number of customers at a faster pace  they will be able to use the mobile  platform to bring efficiency in their  work  SMAC professionals can also use various  analytic tools that will help  organizations gain a stronghold on big  data  additionally SMAC professionals can use  cloud computing knowledge to reduce the  complexity of database management and  storage smack professionals with their  extensive knowledge of each component  can help organizations to reduce costs  and increase overall  efficiency in the next screen we will  focus on the list of lessons covered in  this course this course comprises five  lessons take a look at the lesson names  listed on the screen this concludes the  lesson on overview of smack the next  lesson provides an introduction to smack  wishing you all the luck for this course
 

